    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Look, I'm not asking to ignore anything, I'm just saying we need to be smart about how we frame it so we don't spook them. We can't wait for a whole new formal report, the meeting is in a few days. \n\nIf we mention \"liquefaction risk\" or \"mitigation\" in the main slides, the board is going to start asking a million questions about safety and cost that we aren't ready to answer. Instead of making it a \"risk\" issue, can't we just frame the soil composition as a \"standard coastal geotechnical profile\" that is \"fully compatible with modern deep-foundation engineering\"? Just give me a way to write this summary so the stability of the land is the main takeaway and the technical details stay in the background.",
